<title>INDIA: Indian soybean down, oil up, meal firm.</title>
<headline>Indian soybean down, oil up, meal firm.</headline>
<dateline>INDORE, India 1996-10-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Soybean prices were slightly down on increased arrivals in markets on Tuesday, dealers said.</p>
<p>Prices were down by 50-100 rupees per tonne in markets and plant delivery condition. Arrivals were around 10,000 tonnes in central Indian markets.</p>
<p>Demand from processing plants was good.</p>
<p>Soyoil solvent was up by 100 rupees on limited selling from solvent extraction plants. Soyoil refined was steady and the undertone was steady.</p>
<p>Soymeal and rapeseed extraction prices remained firm on good export demand. Prices of soymeal rose by atleast 20 dollars per tonne within a week. Soymeal yellow was $274-275 per tonne in export.</p>
<p>Rapeseed extraction was $125-127 per tonne in export.</p>
<p>Rapeseed extraction was 4,300 rupees FOR Bedibunder and was 4,250-4,275 rupees FOR Bhavnagar.</p>
